Hows about a 1-Hour Photo Development Shop.  One could walk in and have the
shopkeepers offer to develop your film once every other round (this also, if
the message is long enough with enough --more-- in it gives an impression of the
natives offering unwanted services at less than favorable prices, anthe hassle
Tourists should receive) and have a "NAME.SNP" file produced in the Hack
directory.  As pictures are taken, the player should make a comment as to what's
going on.

The content of this file would be all the pictures taken by a particular player
and successfully developed.

eg.

: In a Room.  A stunned little dog.                     :
: In a Room.  An Orc, dazed but shouting for help.      :
: In a Corridor.  A Floating Eye.                       :
: In a Room.  A wall.                                   :
: In a Morgue.  A zombie.                               :
: In a Room.  A sleeping nymph.                         :
: In a Room.  A nymph.                                  :
: In a Room.  A dead nymph, a mirror, a pink potion     :
:             my arrows, scrolls and other things.      :
: In a Shop.  A shopkeeper.                             :
: In a Shop.  An angry shopkeeper.                      :
: In a Shop.  He did'nt know I had a wand of death ray. :

etc.

Well I think it'd be a laugh.

In Moria (when I saw someone playing it across the room somewhere) there are
spells and wands etc. which cause explosions when they hit a target or a wall.
I think that that would be pretty neat.  In Moria, it seems you don't take
when a ball explodes around you wich causes 50 odd Hp to anything else!  I'm
not suggesting such a soft option for us proper terminal based RPGers.

I'm awaiting your comments, flames, hitmen etc.

Tim Brown.


